# Allowlist of scripts/check-no-public-network-in-tests.py: test-source lines that name a public
# server or a non-local address but do no I/O with it.
#
#   <path> | <count> | <text the line contains> | <reason>
#
# The row allows exactly <count> flagged lines of <path> containing the text: one more fails (a
# new line under an old row), one fewer fails (a stale row). A line that does reach off the
# machine never belongs here: fix the test (a server on loopback in the same process).
rtci-ice/src/agent/agent_rfc6544_mdns_test.rs | 2 | "192.168.0.3: | A test helper named connect that feeds a sans-I/O ICE-TCP agent; no socket
rtci-ice/src/lib.rs | 1 | stun:stun.l.google.com:19302 | Doc-test parsing a URL; no I/O
rtci-mdns/src/message/message_test.rs | 10 | google.com | DNS name parsing and canonicalisation test vectors; no I/O
rtci-shared/src/stream/stream_test.rs | 2 | addr("10.0.0.1:0") | The sans-I/O stream table's connect (a queued command); no socket
src/lib.rs | 4 | stun:stun.l.google.com:19302 | Crate documentation examples marked no_run: compiled, never run
src/peer_connection/configuration/mod.rs | 12 | stun:stun.l.google.com:19302 | Configuration parsing, serialisation and documentation examples of the rtci peer: no driver, nothing resolved or sent
src/peer_connection/configuration/mod.rs | 2 | global.stun.twilio.com | Configuration parsing, serialisation and documentation examples of the rtci peer: no driver, nothing resolved or sent
src/peer_connection/mod.rs | 2 | stun:stun.l.google.com:19302 | Documentation examples on the rtci peer's configuration: no driver, so the name is never resolved and nothing is sent
tests/testenv/mod.rs | 1 | s.connect("224.0.0.251:5353") | UDP connect to the mDNS group only picks the egress interface (a UDP connect sends nothing); real-network environment only (#[ignore] outside it)
